                 L A T E N T  -  8k intro

  title ....... Snow Globe
  type ........ 8k intro, WebGL2, single HTML file (7,673 bytes)
  code ........ Mistral Vibe
  music ....... Mistral Large 4 - original music-box waltz, 96 BPM, 3/4, D major
  harness ..... Mistral Vibe
  runs on ..... Edge / Chrome on Windows, double-click intro.html

  A snow globe on a desk at night, shaken to the waltz. Inside
  the glass a cabin with a lit window and a smoking chimney, two
  pines, a lantern, and snow that swirls on every beat of the
  shake and settles when the globe is set down. Outside: a warm
  lamp, a moonlit window, moonlight on the varnish, and the
  globe's own reflection in the desk. 135 seconds, 72 bars.

  The shake is one envelope shared by picture and sound: the
  globe's tilt, the snow's swirl, the camera shake and the
  shaker noise in the soundtrack are all the same SW, so they
  hit together.

  credits: box SDF after I. Quilez, ACES fit by K. Narkowicz,
  hashes by D. Hoskins and M. O'Neill (PCG), FDN reverb after
  Jot & Chaigne. Loader and synth method from Latent's Turbo
  Boost (37) and Wavefolder (27).

